course: dictionary
lesson: 8121
title: Repeat: doing it again
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To repeat means to do or say something again. «Could you repeat that, please?» means please say it one more time.
explain: Look at the words around a word to find its meaning. In «repeat after me», you say the same words the teacher has just said. In «on repeat», something plays again and again.
explain: Maths uses repeat too. A pattern that repeats has the same part again and again, like red, blue, red, blue. A repeating decimal, such as 0.333..., has digits that go on again forever.
fact: To repeat means to do or say something again.
fact: «Repeat after me» means say the same words someone else has just said.
fact: A pattern that repeats has the same part over and over.
fact: A repeating decimal has digits that go on again and again, like 0.333...
fact: A repeat is something shown again, such as a TV show.
exercise: Mrs Lane says, «Could you repeat that, please?» What does she want you to do? | Leave the room quietly | Sing a different song | Write a new story | *Say it again
exercise: The beads go red, blue, red, blue. What repeats? | The colour green only | Nothing, the beads are all different | The beads on the floor | *The pattern red, blue, red, blue
exercise: In 0.333..., what is the repeating part? | *The 3, again and again forever | It does not repeat at all | The dot | 0.33, only once
test: Mr Hill says, «Repeat after me.» What should you do? | Write a new story | Run out of the room | Sing a different song | *Say the same words he says
test: Which word means a TV show that is shown again? | A puzzle | A decimal | *A repeat | A cartoon
exam: In «on repeat», the song plays again and again. What does on repeat mean? | *Again and again | Very quietly | Played backwards | Turned off for good
